 {
  "id": "q_phy001",
  "type": "SCQ",
  "stem": "A uniform solid disc of mass $M$ and radius $R$ rotates about an axis through a point on its rim, perpendicular to its plane. Its moment of inertia about this axis is",
  "images": [],
  "options": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$\\tfrac12 MR^2$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$MR^2$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$\\tfrac32 MR^2$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$2MR^2$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": {
   "keys": [
    "C"
   ]
  },
  "solution": "About the centre, $I_{cm}=\\tfrac12 MR^2$. The rim axis is parallel and at distance $R$, so by the parallel axis theorem\n\n$$I = I_{cm} + MR^2 = \\tfrac12 MR^2 + MR^2 = \\tfrac32 MR^2.$$",
  "solution_source": "in_house",
  "tax": {
   "subject": "PHY",
   "chapter": "PHY.ROT",
   "topics": [
    "PHY.ROT.MOI"
   ],
   "concepts": [
    "parallel_axis"
   ]
  },
