 {
  "id": "q_phy003",
  "type": "SCQ",
  "stem": "A block of mass $2$ kg is lifted vertically through $3$ m at constant speed. Taking $g=10\\ \\text{m s}^{-2}$, the work done by the lifting force is",
  "images": [],
  "options": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$20$ J"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$30$ J"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$60$ J"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$120$ J"
   }
  ],
  "answer": {
   "keys": [
    "C"
   ]
  },
  "solution": "At constant speed the net force is zero, so the lifting force equals the weight $mg=20$ N. Work $=Fd=20\\times 3=60$ J.",
  "solution_source": "in_house",
