 {
  "id": "q_phy007",
  "type": "NVQ",
  "stem": "A block of mass $2$ kg slides down the smooth plane inclined at $30^\\circ$ shown below. Taking $g=10\\ \\text{m s}^{-2}$, its acceleration down the plane, in $\\text{m s}^{-2}$, is\n\n![block on a smooth incline](img:72da92e3bd83a053)",
  "images": [
   {
    "id": "72da92e3bd83a053",
    "w": 659,
    "h": 448,
    "alt": "A block of mass m on a smooth plane inclined at 30 degrees to the horizontal",
    "variants": [
     480,
     659
    ]
   }
  ],
  "answer": {
   "value": 5,
   "tol": 0
  },
  "solution": "With no friction the only component of gravity along the plane gives $ma=mg\\sin30^\\circ$, so $a=10\\times\\tfrac12=5\\ \\text{m s}^{-2}$. The mass cancels.",
