 {
  "id": "q_phy008",
  "type": "SCQ",
  "stem": "In the circuit shown, an ideal $12$ V battery is connected in series with resistors of $4\\ \\Omega$ and $2\\ \\Omega$. The current in the circuit is\n\n![series circuit with 12 V battery](img:3533f734625d29de)",
  "images": [
   {
    "id": "3533f734625d29de",
    "w": 763,
    "h": 391,
    "alt": "A 12 V battery connected in series with a 4 ohm resistor and a 2 ohm resistor",
    "variants": [
     480,
     763
    ]
   }
  ],
  "options": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$0.5$ A"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$1$ A"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$2$ A"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$3$ A"
   }
  ],
  "answer": {
   "keys": [
    "C"
   ]
  },
  "solution": "Resistors in series add: $R=4+2=6\\ \\Omega$. By Ohm's law $I=V/R=12/6=2$ A.",
